Caja does not use glycin; instead, it uses gdk-pixbuf-thumbnailer to 
generate thumnails. Hence, this "-compat" package, which ships:

  /usr/bin/gdk-pixbuf-thumbnailer
  /usr/share/thumbnailers/gdk-pixbuf-thumbnailer.thumbnailer

In addition, Caja will get confised by the presence of glycin's
thumbnailers, so remove these (at your own risk):

  /usr/share/thumbnailers/glycin-image-rs.thumbnailer
  /usr/share/thumbnailers/glycin-svg.thumbnailer

Then, consider adding the following to /etc/pkgadd.conf:

  INSTALL		^usr/share/thumbnailers/glycin-image-rs\.thumbnailer	NO
  INSTALL		^usr/share/thumbnailers/glycin-svg\.thumbnailer		NO
